TESTSUITE "RECEXPL record-expectations proof"

*> WS-NET-TOTAL is left open on purpose (simulating a cobol-parser
*> gen-fixtures tier-3 stub: a COMPUTE-derived value the static generator
*> would not have asserted a value for) so `run --record-expectations` has
*> something real to fill in. See
*> docs/2026-08-04-record-expectations-design.md.
TESTCASE "doubles a quantity of 20"
    MOCK CALL "DISCOUNT"
        MOVE 5 TO WS-DISCOUNT-CODE
    END-MOCK
    MOVE 20 TO WS-QTY
    PERFORM CALC-TOTALS
    EXPECT WS-DISCOUNT-CODE TO BE 5
    *> STUB EXPECT WS-NET-TOTAL -- case one

TESTCASE "doubles a quantity of 7"
    MOCK CALL "DISCOUNT"
        MOVE 5 TO WS-DISCOUNT-CODE
    END-MOCK
    MOVE 7 TO WS-QTY
    PERFORM CALC-TOTALS
    EXPECT WS-DISCOUNT-CODE TO BE 5
    *> STUB EXPECT WS-NET-TOTAL -- case two
